---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — LevelChineseNews"
  description="Why we built LevelChineseNews: bridging intermediate reading and native-level Chinese news."
>
  <main class="inner prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      Hi, thanks for your interest in our little project. I started learning Chinese in 2021; the first
      couple hundred vocabulary words came easily from a frequency list. I am heritage Chinese, so I had
      exposure to spoken language, but reading required active study. I set out to read Chinese at a
      native level within five years. After the basics, there is a real gap between native-level books
      and articles and what intermediate (HSK4/5) learners can read without looking up every other
      sentence.
    </p>
    <p>
      I decided to build LevelChineseNews to bridge that gap—starting around Chinese New Year 2026. The
      first version had pinyin and segmentation, a basic CEDICT, and Pleco integration. Simple tools made
      even complex native-level articles feel approachable. Since then I have added sentence-level
      translations, AI-assisted learning features, and more media sources so I can read what I already
      care about.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are preparing for internal beta with a few dozen users. If you are an intermediate Chinese
      learner and want to try new tools while reading real, native content, I would love your feedback on
      what to build next. Reach me at <a href="mailto:shanhui.dev@proton.me">shanhui.dev@proton.me</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
